  "authors": [],
  "body": {
    "comment": "I vote NO on \"Withdraw 11,787,063 ada for the OpenZeppelin Stack administered by Intersect\". OpenZeppelin's record is real, but the treasury is asked to pay twice for the same public good: IO's already funded Developer Experience Initiative covers an OpenZeppelin-style Aiken contracts library, its public repo is still being updated, and this proposal publishes no gap analysis or division of labour. The core technical choice is deferred rather than resolved - the language is picked only after funding - so cost and interoperability cannot be judged. The ask is fixed in ada at a USD 0.16 reference rate while ada trades near USD 0.25, adding roughly USD 1M of converted value with no stated rule for the surplus or conversion fee, and the 500M Net Change Limit cited for compliance was rejected with 62.35% support. I expect a leaner, phased resubmission - library, security and standards first - that names the language, shows the gap and returns any surplus."
  },
  "hashAlgorithm": "blake2b-256"
}